{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"The revised timing path still goes through the hazard unit because load-use detection reads IF’s redirect-muxed instruction. I’ll make that comparison use raw instruction-memory operand fields only when `imem_ready` is high. A redirecting EX instruction cannot itself be a load, and an imem stall masks unavailable instruction data, so this removes redirect from hazard feedback without changing hazard decisions."}}
