 to `a_hi + b_hi + 1`. This avoids cascading a second add onto\n  the high-half adder. Operation decode, pipeline timing, and other ALU ops\n  are unchanged.\n- No tests or other RTL modules were changed.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed and 0 failed, using the automatically selected\n  single-retirement wrapper.\n- ALU unit test: pass (`1 passed`).\n- Cosim: pass for selftest and CoreMark (`2 ELFs tested`) with `NRET=1`, which\n  matches `cores/bench/core.yaml`. The default `make cosim` build uses\n  `NRET=2` and fails to compile this single-retirement core; setting\n  `NRET=1` resolves that harness configuration issue.\n- Gowin timing: the original `a + b` measured 70.461 MHz in a baseline run;\n  this carry-select version measured 71.254 MHz. These are single-option\n  measurements, so the gain is modest and may vary with placement.\n\n## Concerns\n\nThe measured frequency increase is small, and the carry-select implementation\nuses slightly more logic in the reported timing run. Full multi-placement FPGA\nfitness remains the definitive comparison.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
