{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented registered EX/MEM redirects. The interlock holds fetch and clears younger work during resolution; the registered target redirects PC on the following cycle, even during an instruction-bus stall. Not-taken branches also incur an interlock bubble.\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench`: passed. The literal wildcard command hit the existing `core_pkg.sv` source-order requirement; the Makefile lint target orders it first.\n- Formal: **53 passed, 0 failed** with `run_all.sh` auto-selecting the `nret: 1` wrapper.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed, both ELF programs.\n- FPGA evaluation: passed; median Fmax **51.852 MHz**, fitness **101.98**. The worst path now runs through forwarding and the ALU to a dmem output.\n\nChanges are in [core.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1/cores/bench/rtl/core.sv), [ex_stage.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1/cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv), [hazard_unit.sv](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1/cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv), and related pipeline files. Verification details and the `NRET=1` build requirement are recorded in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260929-002-r3s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)."}}
