{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git status --short --untracked-files=all && git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Change\n\nAdded `pc_plus4` to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles. IF computes it once from\nthe current fetch PC, uses it for normal sequential fetch advancement, and\npasses it through decode and the existing operand register to EX. EX uses the\ncarried value for redirect fall-through, `pc_next` retirement metadata, and\nJAL/JALR link writeback.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nNo functional deviations from the hypothesis. The value adds 32 bits at each\nof the ID/EX and operand pipeline boundaries. The current timing report's\nworst listed path is still an ALU path; no before/after timing comparison was\nrun in this turn.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks, using the auto-detected NRET=1 wrapper.\n- Cosimulation: pass, both ELF checks. The initial default `make cosim`\n  attempted NRET=2 and failed to compile against this core's NRET=1 ports;\n  rerunning with `NRET=1` passed.\n- Gowin timing: place option 0 reported Fmax 75.628 MHz; the worst listed\n  path was operand immediate to EX ALU result at 18.517 ns.\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
