= branch_unsigned_lt;\n+      BR_BGEU: branch_cond = !branch_unsigned_lt;\n       default: branch_cond = 1'b0;\n     endcase\n     branch_taken  = in.ctrl.is_branch && branch_cond;\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Change\n\nIn `rtl/ex_stage.sv`, branch resolution now computes one equality result and\none unsigned less-than result from the forwarded operands. Signed less-than\nuses the sign-bit correction `(rs1[31] != rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_lt`.\nBEQ/BNE use equality and its complement; BGE/BGEU use the complements of the\nsigned/unsigned less-than results. Branch latency and redirect behavior are\nunchanged.\n\nNo deviations from the hypothesis were needed.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed.\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`):\n  passed, 53 checks and 0 failures.\n- Gowin timing (`make timing TARGET=bench`): passed. Reported Fmax was\n  74.851 MHz. The longest reported path still runs from a registered operand\n  through EX, fetch, decode, and the register file.\n- Cosim: passed for both ELF tests when run with `NRET=1`. The default\n  `make cosim TARGET=bench` invocation failed at C++ compilation because the\n  build script defaults to `NRET=2`, while this core exposes its declared\n  single-channel `nret: 1` interface. Rerunning with `NRET=1` matched the\n  existing interface and passed.\n\n## Concern\n\nThe timing run confirms the targeted feedback path remains the longest path;\nthis change did not move the reported critical-path endpoints. Fmax was\n74.851 MHz for the reported placement option.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
