{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '112,165p' cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    end\n  end\n\n  // ── Branch resolve ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  logic        branch_cond;\n  logic        branch_taken;\n  logic        branch_mismatch;\n  logic [31:0] branch_target;\n  logic [13:0] branch_low_sum;\n  logic        branch_inc_hi;\n  logic        branch_dec_hi;\n  logic [18:0] branch_target_hi;\n  logic [31:0] jump_target;\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  logic [31:0] jalr_sum;  // bit 0 deliberately dropped per RV JALR spec\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n\n  always_comb begin\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)\n      BR_BEQ:  branch_cond = (rs1 == rs2);\n      BR_BNE:  branch_cond = (rs1 != rs2);\n      BR_BLT:  branch_cond = ($signed(rs1) <  $signed(rs2));\n      BR_BGE:  branch_cond = ($signed(rs1) >= $signed(rs2));\n      BR_BLTU: branch_cond = (rs1 <  rs2);\n      BR_BGEU: branch_cond = (rs1 >= rs2);\n      default: branch_cond = 1'b0;\n    endcase\n    branch_taken  = in.ctrl.is_branch && branch_cond;\n    branch_mismatch = in.ctrl.is_branch &&\n                      (branch_taken != in.predicted_taken);\n    // B-immediates are signed 13-bit offsets. Add the low 13 bits, then\n    // correct the upper PC field by one when the low sum crosses its\n    // boundary; this keeps the branch redirect off a full-width adder.\n    branch_low_sum = {1'b0, in.pc[12:0]} + {1'b0, in.imm[12:0]};\n    branch_inc_hi = branch_low_sum[13] && !in.imm[12];\n    branch_dec_hi = !branch_low_sum[13] && in.imm[12];\n    branch_target_hi[0] = in.pc[13] ^ branch_inc_hi ^ branch_dec_hi;\n    branch_target = {branch_target_hi, branch_low_sum[12:0]};\n    // JALR clears bit 0 (RV spec); JAL uses imm directly.\n    jalr_sum    = rs1 + in.imm;\n    jump_target = in.ctrl.is_jalr ? {jalr_sum[31:1], 1'b0}\n                                  : (in.pc + in.imm);\n  end\n\n  for (genvar target_bit = 1; target_bit < 19; target_bit++) begin : gen_branch_target_hi\n    assign branch_target_hi[target_bit] = in.pc[13 + target_bit] ^\n      ((branch_inc_hi && (&in.pc[13 +: target_bit])) ||\n       (branch_dec_hi && (~|in.pc[13 +: target_bit])));\n  end\n\n  // ── Misaligned branch / jump target trap ──────────────────────────────\n  // riscv-formal's spec demands rvfi_trap=1 when next_pc is misaligned\n  // (without C extension that means [1:0] != 0). We trap the offending\n  // instruction, suppress the redirect (PC stays linear), and clear\n# Narrow EX branch target adder\n\n## Change\n\nUpdated `rtl/ex_stage.sv` to form branch targets from a 13-bit low sum and\nadjust the upper 19 PC bits by one for signed-immediate underflow or overflow.\nThe branch comparison, redirect behavior, and JAL/JALR target arithmetic are\nunchanged.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nNo architectural deviation. The high-field correction uses bitwise\nincrement/decrement propagation, as in the existing narrow memory-address\nadder. This keeps the branch target modulo-32-bit equivalent to `pc + imm`;\nthe Gowin timing result still shows a path through EX, IF, ID, and the register\nfile, so the complete redirect/decode feedback path remains a concern.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with no warnings.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures, using the auto-detected\n  single-retirement wrapper for `nret: 1`.\n- Cosim: passed for both selftest and CoreMark, including the configured stall\n  scenarios. The direct Makefile build needed `NRET=1` in the environment to\n  match `cores/bench/core.yaml`.\n- Gowin timing, placement option 0: Fmax 68.458 MHz. The worst reported path\n  was `cpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val` through EX, IF, ID, and the register file\n  (19.902 ns, 42 cells).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
