{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"pwd && rg -n \\\"test_alu|rtl/\\\\*|mul_pipeline|verilator --lint|formal/run_all\\\" Makefile cores/bench/test cores/bench -g '\"'!rtl/*.sv'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-002-r10s1\nMakefile:77:\t@echo \"  make lint TARGET=v1     — verilator lint over cores/<TARGET>/rtl/*.sv\"\nMakefile:99:\t  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+$(RTL_DIR) \\\nMakefile:122:\tbash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\nMakefile:130:\tbash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks-deep.cfg\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:137:def test_alu_runner():\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:141:               test_module=\"test_alu\")\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Remove redundant redirect flush in ID\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The divider removed the arithmetic bottleneck; the measured critical path now\\nruns from the register file through EX branch resolution and IF/hazard control\\nback into the ID pipeline register. Redirect already makes IF emit an invalid\\nNOP, while hazard control separately clears the entire ID/EX bundle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The divider removed the arithmetic bottleneck; the measured critical path now\\nruns from the register file through EX branch resolution and IF/hazard control\\nback into the ID pipeline register. Redirect already makes IF emit an invalid\\nNOP, while hazard control separately clears the entire ID/EX bundle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Stop asserting the ID-stage bundle flush for redirects and retain it only for\\nload-use hazards. On a redirect, IF supplies the NOP with valid low, which ID\\ncan capture normally; its benign ADDI-to-x0 controls have no architectural or\\nmemory side effects. This removes the late EX-to-hazard redirect signal from\\nthe wide ID/EX clear mux, shortening the branch feedback path without changing\\nredirect recovery or retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Clear ID/EX for load-use hazards only; rely on IF's invalid NOP for redirects.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"me\n…[2616 of 5688 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:05a0cb835f15a69e]…\nreported path still runs from the register file through ID, EX, IF, hazard, and back into ID.\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n- The redirect NOP still decodes to an ADDI control bundle, but `valid=0`, `rd=x0`, and its memory controls are clear. It cannot retire, write a nonzero register, or access memory.\\n- The measured single-placement Fmax (46.423 MHz) is close to, and slightly below, the core's recorded 46.499 MHz. This run does not demonstrate a timing gain; the evaluator uses a median across placement options.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T20:15:25.769253Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r2s0 (regression, +3.02%): Removing redirect from the wide ID/EX clear condition did not shorten the register-file\\u2192EX-redirect\\u2192IF/hazard\\u2192ID feedback path, so optimize the full redirect feedback cone rather than assuming a narrower bundle mux moves timing.\"}\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:137:def test_alu_runner():\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py:141:               test_module=\"test_alu\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
