{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The timing report exposed one interaction: `if_stage` replaces the incoming instruction with a NOP on redirect, so the newly retimed ID adder still had redirect on its input path. I’m adjusting the fetch bundle so redirect invalidates the instruction through `valid`/the existing ID flush, while only an instruction-memory stall selects the NOP. That keeps wrong-path work from committing and removes redirect from the target adder’s instruction input."}}
