{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The bypass removed the target-adder path, but it also exposed wrong-path instruction bits to more combinational logic and the measured Fmax fell. I’m keeping IF’s original NOP behavior and adding a separate raw instruction field solely for the ID target-immediate calculation, so redirect no longer selects the adder input and the rest of ID sees the same squashed instruction as before."}}
