{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added separate 2-bit saturating direction counters for backward and forward conditional branches in `rtl/if_stage.sv`.\n- Initialized the backward counter to strongly taken (`2'b11`) and the forward counter to strongly not taken (`2'b00`). IF selects a counter using the encoded branch displacement sign and uses its high bit, while retaining branch validation, target alignment qualification, target calculation, and redirect recovery.\n- Added EX resolution outputs for valid branch, displacement class, and actual direction. Training is suppressed for invalid branches and while EX is stalled or held by the divider.\n- Connected EX training signals to IF in `rtl/core.sv`.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed architecture. Each displacement class shares one counter, so unrelated forward branches (and likewise backward branches) can affect each other's predictions. This is the intended area and lookup-depth tradeoff.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: passed with `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`.\n- Formal: passed, 53 checks and 0 failures, with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`.\n- Cosim: passed, 2 ELF workloads, with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`.\n- The first plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` attempt failed at C++ compilation because `test/cosim/build.sh` defaults to NRET=2 unless `NRET` is set. Setting `NRET=1` matched `cores/bench/core.yaml` and passed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
