{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n# Implementation notes\n\n## Changes\n\n- Added a four-entry return-address stack in EX. Valid, non-trapping JAL/JALR\n  writes to x1 or x5 push `pc + 4`; valid ABI-form JALR returns pop. When full,\n  a push drops the oldest entry and retains the newest four.\n- IF recognizes JALR with `imm=0`, `rs1=x1/x5`, and a non-link `rd`. It uses\n  the stack top only when valid and word aligned, redirects fetch immediately,\n  and carries the predicted target through ID/EX and the operand register.\n- EX suppresses return recovery only when the resolved JALR target matches\n  the carried target. If a predicted return resolves to a misaligned target,\n  EX traps the instruction and redirects fetch to `pc + 4` to undo the\n  speculative fetch.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- Stack overflow discards the oldest address rather than wrapping a circular\n  pointer. This preserves the most recent four nested calls.\n- The stack and two target metadata registers add state. Gowin reported 950\n  registers and 73.944 MHz; the existing recorded result is 753 registers and\n  74.129 MHz. The critical paths still begin at `u_operand/reg_q.imm_4_s0` and\n  do not cross the return stack. The measured Fmax is slightly lower.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass, 53 checks. The first run found `pc_fwd_ch0` failing when a\n  return prediction was followed by a misaligned resolved JALR target. Added\n  recovery to `pc + 4`; the next run passed all checks.\n- Cosim: pass for selftest and CoreMark using `NRET=1`, matching\n  `cores/bench/core.yaml`. The unqualified `make cosim TARGET=bench` first\n  attempted the build with the harness default `NRET=2`, which does not match\n  this core's RVFI ports.\n- Gowin timing: pass; Fmax 73.944 MHz across the requested timing flow.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the four-entry EX return stack and IF prediction for aligned ABI-form returns. EX suppresses recovery only on an exact target match and recovers to `pc+4` if a predicted return traps for misalignment.\n\n- Verilator lint: passed\n- Formal: 53 checks passed\n- Cosim: passed with `NRET=1` (matching `core.yaml`)\n- Gowin timing: 73.944 MHz\n\nRecorded details and the initial formal fix in [implementation_notes.md](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6-luna_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260930-003-r9s2/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md). The measured Fmax is slightly below the existing recorded 74.129 MHz."}}
