{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -8 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && cat cores/bench/core.yaml && cat cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20260930-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Predict aligned backward branches with a narrow target path\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark loop back-edges currently redirect from EX and flush younger\\ninstructions. Prior branch predictors recovered some of those cycles, but\\ntheir fetch-time table lookup or full-width target logic reduced Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark loop back-edges currently redirect from EX and flush younger\\ninstructions. Prior branch predictors recovered some of those cycles, but\\ntheir fetch-time table lookup or full-width target logic reduced Fmax.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a static backward-taken, forward-not-taken predictor for valid,\\naligned conditional branches. Compute the B-type target using a 13-bit\\nlow-part sum and sign/carry-controlled upper increment or decrement,\\navoiding a full 32-bit fetch-path adder. Carry the predicted-taken bit\\nwith the instruction and make EX redirect on an outcome mismatch, while\\nretaining the existing misaligned-target trap behavior. The smaller target\\ncone may preserve the loop-recovery IPC gain without the timing penalty\\nseen in earlier predictors.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the predicted-taken bit in the fetch and decoded instruction bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predict eligible backward branches and form their targets with narrow low-part addition and upper adjustment logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Preserve the fetch prediction bit into the execute-stage payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Redirect conditional branches only when resolved direction disagrees with prediction, preserving misalignment traps.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the predicted-taken bit in the fetch and decoded instruction bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"descrip\n…[23936 of 27008 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:715e51cade2aaf48]…\n]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T23:01:25.321633Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r10s0 (regression, -4.95%): Selecting signedness on the inputs of one widened 33\\u00d733 multiplier adds operation-dependent control to the multiply path, so source-level sharing may lose to separately expressed RV32M products in FPGA timing or mapping.\"}\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 74.129\n  lut4: 2743\n  ff: 753\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20260930-003-r7s2\n  updated: '2026-09-29T22:18:30.289391Z'\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
