{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The current post-divider critical path closes through EX redirect, IF, hazard control, and back into ID. I’m targeting that feedback specifically: IF already supplies an invalid NOP on redirect, so ID’s separate redirect clear of the whole pipeline bundle appears redundant and keeps the late branch signal on a wide register-input path."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses && cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r2s0.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260929-001-r2s0\ntitle: \\\"Remove redundant redirect flush in ID\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The divider removed the arithmetic bottleneck; the measured critical path now\n  runs from the register file through EX branch resolution and IF/hazard control\n  back into the ID pipeline register. Redirect already makes IF emit an invalid\n  NOP, while hazard control separately clears the entire ID/EX bundle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Stop asserting the ID-stage bundle flush for redirects and retain it only for\n  load-use hazards. On a redirect, IF supplies the NOP with valid low, which ID\n  can capture normally; its benign ADDI-to-x0 controls have no architectural or\n  memory side effects. This removes the late EX-to-hazard redirect signal from\n  the wide ID/EX clear mux, shortening the branch feedback path without changing\n  redirect recovery or retirement behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Clear ID/EX for load-use hazards only; rely on IF's invalid NOP for redirects.\\\"\nEOF\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-001-r2s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
