{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260929-003-r6s2.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20260929-003-r6s2\ntitle: \\\"Register-ahead branch target prediction\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Earlier static, BTB, and return-stack predictors regressed after adding\n  combinational predictor work to the fetch/redirect path. Taken loop branches\n  still cost recovery cycles, so prediction can improve CoreMark if lookup delay\n  is removed from the PC selection path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small tagged target table with direction state, but pipeline its lookup\n  one fetch step ahead: whenever the PC advances, capture the BTB prediction for\n  the selected next PC alongside that PC. The current PC then uses registered\n  prediction metadata to select a target, keeping tag comparison and table\n  selection out of the same-cycle PC feedback mux. Train entries from resolved\n  branches and jumps, and preserve the existing EX recovery on a prediction\n  miss. This should recover cycles on repeated taken loop branches without the\n  fetch-path delay of a combinational BTB lookup.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry prediction metadata aligned with the current fetch PC through retirement resolution.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Add a small tagged direction/target table and register its lookup for the selected next fetch PC.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry the fetch prediction metadata with the decoded instruction.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Resolve prediction hits against actual next PC and expose branch/jump training information.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Connect EX resolution and predictor training to the fetch stage.\\\"\nYAML\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
