{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(x) for x in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")];\nfor x in rows:\n if x.get(\\\"id\\\") in [\\\"hyp-20260929-001-r3s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20260930-001-r7s0\\\"]:\n  print(\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"title\\\"]); print(x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"].get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\")); print(\\\"critical\\\",x.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"\n hyp-20260929-001-r3s0 Share branch comparison logic\nIn EX, compute equality once and an unsigned less-than once, derive signed\nless-than from the operand sign bits and the unsigned result, then select\nBEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU from those shared predicates. Complement the shared\npredicate for BNE, BGE, and BGEU. This preserves branch semantics while\navoiding duplicate 32-bit comparison cones in the critical redirect path.\n\ncritical {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_28_s1', 'slack_ns': -17.273, 'arrival_ns': 27.568, 'logic_cells': 47, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\n\n hyp-20260930-001-r7s0 Share branch comparison logic\nExpress all six RV32I branch conditions using one unsigned less-than\ncomparison, one equality comparison, and sign-bit correction for signed\nordering. Derive greater-or-equal conditions as complements of the\ncorresponding less-than result. This should share comparator work and\nreduce the branch-resolution delay feeding redirect and fetch, with no\nchange to pipeline latency, branch semantics, or instruction throughput.\n\ncritical {'from': 'cpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s196', 'slack_ns': -8.36, 'arrival_ns': 18.654, 'logic_cells': 41, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_rf']}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
