tructs the J-immediate, adds it to PC, aligns the target, and selects it on the fetch-to-PC path; avoiding BTB or direction lookup does not remove the front-end timing cost.\nhyp-20260929-003-r6s2 | Register-ahead branch target prediction | regression | -12.91 | - 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-003-r6s2 (regression, -12.91%): Registering BTB metadata alongside the selected PC moves the lookup off the PC feedback mux but leaves a fetch-cycle tag/target path, while wrong predictions still need EX recovery, so a lookup register alone may not repay predictor cost in CoreMark.\nhyp-20260930-002-r9s1 | Register the fetch-to-decode boundary | regression | -0.61 | - 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r9s1 (regression, -0.61%): A registered IF/ID buffer cleared on EX redirect adds a fetch-restart cycle for mispredicted control transfers, so backward-branch prediction must cover enough of CoreMark's redirects to repay that recovery cost.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
