{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"jq -r 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260930-001-r8s0\\\") | {title, hypothesis, changes, fmax_mhz, cycles, delta_pct, critical_path, implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"title\": \"Gate dependency stalls by source use\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The hazard unit compares both encoded register fields for every valid instruction. For OP-IMM and load instructions, rs2 bits are immediate bits, so a matching older destination can insert an unnecessary bubble; instructions with no register sources can also stall unnecessarily.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Decode source-use classes from the ID/EX opcode and gate the execute-result and load-use comparisons with them: R-type, store, and branch instructions use both sources; OP-IMM, load, and JALR use rs1 only; other opcodes use neither. This should remove false dependency bubbles in CoreMark without adding a pipeline stage, while preserving waits whenever an instruction actually consumes the producer's value.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Connect the ID/EX instruction word to hazard detection for source-use classification.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Gate both execute-result and load-use dependency comparisons by decoded rs1/rs2 usage.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Connect the ID/EX instruction word to hazard detection for source-use classification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Gate both execute-result and load-use dependency comparisons by decoded rs1/rs2 usage.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 74.565,\n