 show a path from execute through fetch and decode back to the register file, with branch resolution feeding that feedback cone. The EX branch case currently expresses equality and signed and unsigned order comparisons independently, which can leave several wide comparator networks on the redirect path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Route branch instructions through a shared subtract operation and derive equality and unsigned borrow from its extended difference; derive signed less-than from the subtract sign and overflow bits. Use these shared flags for BEQ, BNE, BLT, BGE, BLTU, and BGEU. Reusing one FPGA carry-chain subtraction should reduce duplicated comparison logic and shorten the EX-to-redirect path without changing pipeline latency or branch behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Select subtraction for branch instructions so their operands enter the shared arithmetic path.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Expose zero, unsigned-borrow, and signed-less flags from one extended subtraction result.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve branch conditions from the shared subtract flags rather than independent relational operators.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
