etaining EX/MEM priority, and select each EX operand with masked terms for the register-file value and both bypass sources. This can remove the encoded-select decode from the critical wide mux while preserving x0 and freshest-writer behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit one-hot EX/MEM and MEM/WB matc\n…[147490 of 150562 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4433db5e9014b626]…\nwhile retaining static fallback prediction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Provide the resolving branch PC and outcome needed to train the expanded table.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect branch resolution training to the 32-entry fetch predictor.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 138.71, \"delta_pct\": -4.92, \"vs_baseline\": 1044.47, \"fmax_mhz\": 68.95, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4970718, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3079, \"ff\": 829, \"seeds\": [73.012, 68.95, 68.95], \"perturbations\": [[0, 73.012, 16], [1, 68.95, 16], [2, 68.95, 16]], \"lutram\": 20, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s195\", \"slack_ns\": -8.696, \"arrival_ns\": 18.991, \"logic_cells\": 41, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T02:31:56.943567Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
