{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x=json.loads(line)\n if x.get('id') in ('hyp-20260929-001-r2s0','hyp-20260930-001-r8s0'):\n  print(json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260929-001-r2s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Remove redundant redirect flush in ID\",\n  \"category\": \"micro_opt\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The divider removed the arithmetic bottleneck; the measured critical path now\\nruns from the register file through EX branch resolution and IF/hazard control\\nback into the ID pipeline register. Redirect already makes IF emit an invalid\\nNOP, while hazard control separately clears the entire ID/EX bundle.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The divider removed the arithmetic bottleneck; the measured critical path now\\nruns from the register file through EX branch resolution and IF/hazard control\\nback into the ID pipeline register. Redirect already makes IF emit an invalid\\nNOP, while hazard control separately clears the entire ID/EX bundle.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Stop asserting the ID-stage bundle flush for redirects and retain it only for\\nload-use hazards. On a redirect, IF supplies the NOP with valid low, which ID\\ncan capture normally; its benign ADDI-to-x0 controls have no architectural or\\nmemory side effects. This removes the late EX-to-hazard redirect signal from\\nthe wide ID/EX clear mux, shortening the branch feedback path without changing\\nredirect recovery or retirement behavior.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Clear ID/EX for load-use hazards only; rely on IF's invalid NOP for redirects.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 7,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Clear ID/EX for load-use hazards only; rely on IF's invalid NOP for redirects.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 106.65,\n  \"delta_pct\": 3.02,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 779.95,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 47.906,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 4491817,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 2650,\n  \"ff\": 631,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    46.423,\n    47.906,\n    47.906\n  ],\n  \"p\n…[5270 of 8342 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6eb57f89d3a72fe1]…\nd load-use dependency comparisons by decoded rs1/rs2 usage.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 147.6,\n  \"delta_pct\": 1.17,\n  \"vs_baseline\": 1117.82,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 74.565,\n  \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06,\n  \"cycles\": 5051958,\n  \"iterations\": 10,\n  \"lut4\": 2773,\n  \"ff\": 760,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    68.966,\n    74.565,\n    74.565\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      68.966,\n      16\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      74.565,\n      9\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      74.565,\n      9\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lutram\": 8,\n  \"bsram\": 6,\n  \"dsp\": 6,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s196\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -9.5,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 19.794,\n    \"logic_cells\": 41,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\",\n      \"cpu/u_rf\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"logic_levels\": 16,\n  \"formal_passed\": true,\n  \"cosim_passed\": true,\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T22:34:08.142789Z\",\n  \"slot\": 0,\n  \"round_id\": 8\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"mkdir -p cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\ncat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r15s0.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Decode register-file reads one-hot\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  Recent timing reports repeatedly cross EX, IF, ID, and the register file, and several identify register-file state as the endpoint. The two asynchronous reads currently use variable-indexed array selection, which can synthesize into deep address mux trees. A shared one-hot decode for each read port may map those selections into shallower local LUT logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the variable-indexed asynchronous reads with full 32-entry one-hot address decoders and masked reductions over the register words. Keep x0 reads hardwired to zero, retain the same-cycle write-first bypass, and preserve the synchronous single-write behavior. This keeps the pipeline and instruction timing unchanged while attempting to shorten the register-file selection cone on the recurring critical path. Unlike a banked read, the full decode avoids selecting among intermediate bank outputs; the FPGA mapping will determine whether the extra decode fanout pays off.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \\\"Implement each asynchronous read as a full one-hot decoded masked reduction while preserving x0 and write-first bypass semantics.\\\"\nEOF\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-001-r15s0.yaml\ngit status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
