{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib; print(pathlib.Path(\\\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"\\\\n--- HYPOTHESIS ---\\\\n\\\"); print(pathlib.Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r10s1.yaml\\\").read_text())'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\n--- HYPOTHESIS ---\n\nid: hyp-20260930-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Pipeline the multiply datapath\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current critical path is the registered execute operands through the combinational ALU into EX/MEM. The ALU builds several full-width products in parallel, which can dominate both the execute delay and FPGA arithmetic resources. A dedicated pipelined multiply path can split that depth while leaving the common integer operations on a short path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational M-extension multiplier with a dedicated two-stage multiplier pipeline: form signedness-correct partial products in the first stage and combine them in the second. Route ordinary ALU operations through matching execute-stage registers so the core can still accept one instruction per cycle. Carry instruction metadata through the new boundary, forward completed results from the later execute stage, and interlock only consumers whose producer has not reached that stage. This should shorten the mapped execute critical path without imposing multiply latency on unrelated instructions, improving Fmax while retaining steady-state throughput.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove full-width combinational products and expose the ordinary ALU path separately from multiply operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/mul_pipeline.sv\n    description: \"Add a two-stage, one-result-per-cycle multiply pipeline with RV32M signed and unsigned product handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add pipeline metadata needed to carry multiply operation, operands or partial products, and instruction identity across the execute boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route multiply requests into the pipelined unit and align ordinary execute results and control metadata with its output stage.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the added execute stage while preserving in-order memory requests and retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Hold dependent instructions until the pipelined multiply result is available while allowing independent instructions to advance.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Forward the completed execute-stage result with correct youngest-producer priority.\"\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
