rget-only BTB treats every exact-PC hit as taken, so mixed-outcome conditional branches lose direction history and can repeatedly mispredict before not-taken resolution invalidates their entries.\n- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-001-r4s0 (regression, -0.97%): Splitting the 32-bit branch comparison into byte predicates still \n…[57170 of 60242 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ed258810e1f78ba7]…\nonce.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 136.23, \"delta_pct\": -6.62, \"vs_baseline\": 1024.01, \"fmax_mhz\": 69.219, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 5081214, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2707, \"ff\": 785, \"seeds\": [71.726, 69.219, 69.219], \"perturbations\": [[0, 71.726, 16], [1, 69.219, 16], [2, 69.219, 16]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s195\", \"slack_ns\": -8.942, \"arrival_ns\": 19.236, \"logic_cells\": 41, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_rf\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T02:12:45.162513Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r13s1 (regression, -6.62%): The DIV_CORRECT state adds a guaranteed completion cycle while EX stays held, so registering divider sign correction needs enough measured timing gain to repay even this divider-only CoreMark latency.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
