, +0.27%): Splitting ADD across the operand/EX boundary puts a forwarded-operand adder before the register while retaining upper-half addition and result selection in EX, so added arithmetic and muxing can outweigh reduced carry depth; check both stage paths after mapping.\nhyp-20260929-002-r6s1\tBypass ready execute results into operands\tregression\t-0.14\tcpu/u_operand/reg_q.pc_5_s0\tdmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\t- 2026-09-29 hyp-20260929-002-r6s\n…[1596 of 4668 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6f91975b5562af4c]…\nng stalls can outweigh the multiply timing gain.\nhyp-20260930-002-r11s1\tBank the asynchronous register file\tregression\t-13.87\tcpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\tcpu/u_id/reg_q.rs2_val_13_s0\t\nhyp-20260930-002-r12s1\tRetiming branch comparison into operand stage\tregression\t-4.08\tcpu/u_ex/u_div/quotient_q_31_s0\tcpu/u_ex/u_div/result_30_s0\t- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r12s1 (regression, -4.08%): Computing the 32-bit branch result after youngest-producer forwarding places both muxing and comparison on the operand-stage register input path, so moving compare work out of EX can shift the critical path upstream instead of shortening it.\nhyp-20260930-002-r13s1\tPipeline divider result correction\tregression\t-6.62\tcpu/u_operand/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\tcpu/u_rf/regs_ER_s195\t- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r13s1 (regression, -6.62%): The DIV_CORRECT state adds a guaranteed completion cycle while EX stays held, so registering divider sign correction needs enough measured timing gain to repay even this divider-only CoreMark latency.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
