{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-002-r8s1.yaml <<'EOF'\nid: hyp-20260930-002-r8s1\ntitle: \\\"Decouple redirect validity from fetched instruction\\\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion's measured worst path runs from the registered operand through EX and IF into ID and the register file. A late branch redirect currently selects a NOP on the IF instruction bus, so redirect control propagates through decode and register-file read selection even though ID is flushed on that same redirect.\nhypothesis: |\n  Separate the fetched instruction payload from redirect validity. Keep the existing NOP substitution for instruction-memory stalls, but let a redirect leave the fetched payload untouched while marking it invalid and relying on the existing ID and operand flushes to discard it. This removes the redirect-controlled instruction mux from the EX-to-ID/register-file path while preserving wrong-path suppression and bus-stall behavior, potentially improving Fmax without adding branch bubbles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Add an explicit instruction-memory-stall input and substitute NOP only for that stall; keep redirect validity and flush behavior while removing redirect selection from the fetched instruction payload.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Connect \"'!io_imemReady as the explicit fetch-stall qualifier so redirect and instruction-memory-stall behavior remain distinct.\"\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
