a_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the prediction bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Predict aligned backward conditional branches taken and redirect fetch to their target.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the fetch prediction bit into the EX-stage pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \n…[104338 of 107410 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6be9a8e046987495]…\n indexed valid/counter selection adds delay to the fetch-to-PC path, so learning forward-branch bias must save enough redirects to repay that lookup cost.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-001-r13s0 (regression, -3.13%): Carrying IF's PC+4 through ID/EX regressed despite removing EX increments, suggesting the 32-bit pipeline payload can cost more in state and routing than recomputing a constant increment when that adder is not proven critical.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-002-r13s1 (regression, -6.62%): The DIV_CORRECT state adds a guaranteed completion cycle while EX stays held, so registering divider sign correction needs enough measured timing gain to repay even this divider-only CoreMark latency.\n- 2026-09-30 hyp-20260930-003-r13s2 (regression, -0.45%): Two global 2-bit counters by displacement sign regress slightly because unrelated forward branches share and can cancel one learned bias, while IF still adds direction selection; class-wide history must save enough redirects to beat static backward-taken prediction.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
