{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') in ['hyp-20260930-003-r7s2','hyp-20260930-003-r11s2','hyp-20260930-003-r12s2','hyp-20260930-003-r13s2']:\n  print('\\\\n###', d['id'], d['title'])\n  print(d['hypothesis'].get('hypothesis',''))\n  print(d.get('implementation_notes','')[:2000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/if_stage.sv\n//\n// Instruction fetch stage. Holds the PC register; the IF/ID payload\n// (pc + instr + valid) is *combinational* — there is no separate IF/ID\n// flop in this microarchitecture, the next-stage's ID/EX register\n// captures everything one cycle later.\n//\n// On flush or redirect, the instruction emitted to ID is forced to NOP\n// (`0x00000013` = ADDI x0,x0,0). This prevents the hazard unit from\n// observing a real rs1/rs2 from a wrong-path instruction and inserting\n// a spurious load-use stall the cycle after a taken branch.\n//\n// Latency:        PC-reg update is synchronous; output is combinational.\n// RVFI fields:    feeds pc_rdata (via ID/EX/MEM/WB) and pc_wdata (via\n//                 EX-stage redirect).\nmodule if_stage (\n  input  logic              clock,\n  input  logic              reset,\n  input  logic              stall,            // hold PC (load-use)\n  input  logic              flush,            // emit NOP into ID this cycle\n  input  logic              redirect,         // EX has resolved a branch/jump\n  input  logic [31:0]       redirect_target,\n  output logic [31:0]       imem_addr,\n  input  logic [31:0]       imem_data,\n  output if_id_t  out\n);\n\n  localparam logic [31:0] RESET_PC = 32'h0000_0000;\n\n  logic [31:0] pc;\n  logic [31:0] next_pc;\n  logic [12:0] branch_imm_low;\n  logic [13:0] branch_low_sum;\n  logic        branch_inc_hi;\n  logic        branch_dec_hi;\n  logic [18:0] branch_target_hi;\n  logic [31:0] branch_target;\n  logic        valid_branch;\n  logic        predicted_taken;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    branch_imm_low = {imem_data[31], imem_data[7], imem_data[30:25],\n                      imem_data[11:8], 1'b0};\n    branch_low_sum = {1'b0, pc[12:0]} + {1'b0, branch_imm_low};\n    branch_inc_hi = branch_low_sum[13] && !imem_data[31];\n    branch_dec_hi = !branch_low_sum[13] && imem_data[31];\n    branch_target_hi[0] = pc[13] ^ branch_inc_hi ^ branch_dec_hi;\n    valid_branch = (imem_data[6:0] == 7'b1100011) &&\n                   (imem_data[14:12] != 3'b010) &&\n                   (imem_\n…[2967 of 6039 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7cc78af2769d99d4]…\nigned conditional branches. Keep the existing target\ncalculation and EX misprediction recovery. Learning the direction of common\nforward and mixed-bias branches should avoid repeated redirect bubbles while\navoiding a BTB target array or additional target arithmetic in the fetch path.\n\n\n\n### hyp-20260930-003-r13s2 Learn direction by branch direction class\nReplace the static direction decision with two 2-bit saturating counters,\none for backward conditional branches and one for forward conditional\nbranches. Initialize them to strongly taken and strongly not-taken,\nrespectively, so cold behavior matches the current static policy. Train\nthe appropriate counter from each valid branch when it resolves in EX,\nand use the selected counter's high bit in IF while retaining the existing\nbranch validation, alignment qualification, target calculation, and EX\nmisprediction recovery. This learns broad forward-branch bias with only a\nsign-class selection instead of a PC-indexed table, limiting added fetch\ndelay and state.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
