{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r15s2.yaml; git status --short --untracked-files=all'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Learn only forward branch directions\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The 16-entry direction table reduced CoreMark cycles, but its fitness gain\n  stayed below the replacement threshold. Backward loop branches already\n  benefit from the proven static policy, so table state and lookup should be\n  spent only on forward branches whose outcomes that policy cannot learn.\nhypothesis: |\n  Keep aligned backward conditional branches statically predicted taken and\n  use a 16-entry PC-indexed, two-bit saturating table only for aligned forward\n  conditional branches. Initialize each counter weakly not-taken, matching\n  the static forward fallback, so per-entry valid bits are unnecessary.\n  Train counters only from valid forward branches resolving in EX, and retain\n  the existing narrow target calculation and misprediction recovery. This\n  preserves loop back-edge behavior while reducing predictor state and\n  avoiding counter lookups for backward branches; the smaller, selective\n  predictor may retain the learned forward-branch cycle savings with less\n  fetch-path and placement cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the all-branch table with 16 weak-not-taken counters used only for aligned forward conditional branches, preserving static backward-taken prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Export valid forward-branch PC and resolved direction for counter training, suppressing updates while EX is stalled.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the EX forward-branch training signals to the IF direction table.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
