{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260930-003-r9s2.yaml && git status --short'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260930-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Predict ABI returns with a small return stack\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current narrow static predictor removes recovery for aligned backward\n  branches, but JALR returns still wait for EX to redirect the fetch PC. CoreMark\n  makes repeated calls and returns, and return targets follow a predictable\n  nesting pattern that can be captured without a fetch-path adder or BTB lookup.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small four-entry return-address stack updated when valid, non-trapping\n  JAL/JALR call and return instructions resolve in EX. In IF, recognize the\n  common ABI return form (JALR with zero immediate, x1 or x5 as rs1, and a\n  non-link rd), and predict its target from the stack top when valid and\n  instruction-aligned. Carry the predicted target alongside the existing\n  prediction bit and suppress the EX redirect only when the resolved JALR\n  target exactly matches it; otherwise retain normal redirect and trap handling.\n  This should remove return-recovery bubbles without adding target arithmetic\n  or a tag lookup to fetch, while exact target checking preserves recovery when\n  the stack prediction is stale or aliased by control flow.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry a predicted target through IF/ID and ID/EX with the existing prediction metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize aligned ABI returns, select the return-stack target, and redirect fetch while marking the prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Preserve the predicted target in the decoded pipeline register.\"\n  - file: rtl/operand_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the predicted target through the operand register to EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Maintain a four-entry return-address stack, expose its top to IF, and validate predicted JALR targets before suppressing redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the return-stack valid and target signals between EX and IF.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
